From: lumia930-linux
Subject: [PATCH] project: msm8974: raise forced kernel/ramdisk/tags load addresses

applies against Mainline4Lumia/lk2nd, branch martini-support
(https://github.com/Mainline4Lumia/lk2nd/tree/martini-support)

the stock msm8974 forced addresses (kernel 0x00008000, ramdisk
0x02000000, tags 0x01e00000) fall partly below where this phone's
windows firmware actually maps usable ram, and the kernel address
in particular sits on top of the live uefi framebuffer at
0x00400000. moved to the 1520 port's addresses (base 0x10000000),
which sit inside the large RAM region exposed by stock firmware.
these addresses were checked against the device-owned Windows physical
memory map; raw logs and registry dumps are deliberately not published.

same idea as KorelisLabs/lumia-1520-mainline's own
0001-msm8974-raise-forced-load-addresses.patch, reproduced here
against the martini-support branch's current defaults.
---
--- a/project/msm8974.mk
+++ b/project/msm8974.mk
@@ -28,9 +28,9 @@
 #Disable thumb mode
 ENABLE_THUMB := false

-DEFINES += ABOOT_FORCE_KERNEL_ADDR=0x00008000
-DEFINES += ABOOT_FORCE_RAMDISK_ADDR=0x02000000
-DEFINES += ABOOT_FORCE_TAGS_ADDR=0x01e00000
+DEFINES += ABOOT_FORCE_KERNEL_ADDR=0x10008000
+DEFINES += ABOOT_FORCE_RAMDISK_ADDR=0x14000000
+DEFINES += ABOOT_FORCE_TAGS_ADDR=0x13e00000
 DEFINES += ABOOT_FORCE_KERNEL64_ADDR=0x00080000

 ifeq ($(EMMC_BOOT),1)
